WEBVTT


00:00:01.230 --> 00:00:05.040
A square neck line is an attractive
addition to a pullover sweater.

00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:09.560
Finishing a square neck line on
the machine can be a challenge.

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:11.660
Are you up for a challenge?

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:13.070
Well, let's get started.

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:20.360
This tutorial is one of our originals
from way back in 2010 here's a requested

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:20.990
update.

00:00:21.950 --> 00:00:26.900
Please forgive the mashup of older
video, different lighting and voice.

00:00:29.029 --> 00:00:34.519
We're creating a neat finish for a
square neck line using the Knit it Now.

00:00:34.519 --> 00:00:37.940
Practice square neck line
pattern, knit a small swatch.

00:00:38.739 --> 00:00:42.070
Basically you want to end up with
a shape that looks like this.

00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:48.360
Now, if this were a round neck to knit a
basic band, I'd hang the neck edge back on

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:50.040
the machine with the wrong side facing.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:57.330
I'd knit maybe six rows, knit, turning row
and knit six more rows to finish the band.

00:00:57.990 --> 00:01:00.420
But wait, I don't want around neck.

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:06.330
When you fold back the turning row to
complete the band, the problem's really

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:06.900
clear.

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:12.390
There's a bunch of extra fabric where the
corner should be for the square neckline.

00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:15.120
Now there'd be no problem
if this were hand knitting.

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:20.970
We'd simply place markers at the corners,
and as we knit the band, we'd knit three

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:28.320
together to make a neat, miter decrease
or double decrease at the corner, but knit

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:31.590
three together on the
machine isn't as easy.

00:01:33.195 --> 00:01:39.015
Follow along as we work center double
decreases to create the public side of our

00:01:39.015 --> 00:01:40.005
square band.

00:01:41.775 --> 00:01:45.045
A mitered band is a beautiful
finish to a square neck line.

00:01:46.035 --> 00:01:50.925
You'll work double decreases on the public
side of the band manually moving the

00:01:50.925 --> 00:01:55.845
stitches and working short rows on
the facing side for a nice finish.

00:01:56.715 --> 00:02:01.305
I've started with the sample
neck line casting on 70 stitches.

00:02:01.725 --> 00:02:05.655
Knit for 30 rows, bind
off or remove the center.

00:02:05.655 --> 00:02:07.155
30 stitches on waste yarn.

00:02:08.144 --> 00:02:12.195
Knit 30 more rows on each side,
binding off each shoulder.

00:02:12.945 --> 00:02:15.075
Block your swatch to make
it easier to work with.

00:02:16.005 --> 00:02:19.725
The upper image used waste yard
to hold the center front stitches.

00:02:20.144 --> 00:02:23.954
You can see that it gives a much smoother
finish than the lower image, which was

00:02:23.954 --> 00:02:25.905
bound off before starting the band.

00:02:27.179 --> 00:02:31.799
Start the band by hanging the garment
with the private or the wrong side facing.

00:02:35.980 --> 00:02:38.230
After you hang the last
of the center stitches.

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:41.470
Use a pencil to Mark the next
needle on the needle bed.

00:02:42.250 --> 00:02:43.769
This will be the start of the miter.

00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:46.000
Do this on both sides.

00:02:47.709 --> 00:02:52.959
Now finish hanging the side neck stitches
being careful to pick up the whole stitch.

00:02:53.769 --> 00:02:55.060
Hang both sides.

00:02:56.445 --> 00:03:02.055
Then at garment tension knit
one row to start the miter.

00:03:02.055 --> 00:03:07.905
Start on the left side of the bed,
transfer each stitch right and left to the

00:03:07.905 --> 00:03:08.715
Mark needle.

00:03:09.675 --> 00:03:14.835
The Mark needle will have three stitches,
transfer all three stitches to the right

00:03:15.135 --> 00:03:16.815
or towards the center of the bed.

00:03:17.565 --> 00:03:19.515
You'll have two empty needles.

00:03:20.415 --> 00:03:24.465
Transfer each of the side neck
stitches, two needles to the right.

00:03:24.975 --> 00:03:26.505
Filling the empty needles.

00:03:43.055 --> 00:03:45.205
Use whatever tool is comfortable for you.

00:03:45.415 --> 00:03:49.315
A multi- stitch transfer tool
or a Garter bar is handy here.

00:03:59.035 --> 00:04:01.405
Repeat the shaping for the other side.

00:04:02.035 --> 00:04:05.965
Transfer one stitch right and
left to the marked needle.

00:04:06.985 --> 00:04:09.715
Transfer all three stitches to the left.

00:04:12.085 --> 00:04:16.255
Fill the empty needles with the remaining
side neck stitches, using the tool of your

00:04:16.255 --> 00:04:16.825
choice.

00:04:18.090 --> 00:04:22.500
When you finish the transfers on both
sides, knit one row, you will have

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:24.810
decreased a total of four stitches.

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:28.680
Repeat the double decreased
process six times.

00:04:29.130 --> 00:04:32.790
You'll notice that I've marked my miter
stitch on the needle bed each time.

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:37.590
You'll be able to feel the Ridge of the
miter, but marking the bed comes in handy

00:04:37.650 --> 00:04:39.030
and will be used later.

00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:44.070
Your piece will look like this after
you've transferred and knit six times.

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:49.590
Create a turning row by knitting one row,
at a loser tension or turn the work with

00:04:49.590 --> 00:04:51.930
the garter bar and add a garter Ridge.

00:04:53.220 --> 00:04:55.560
You're now ready to knit the band facing.

00:04:55.650 --> 00:05:00.450
If you knit straight up from here, you'll
have a total of 24 fewer stitches than

00:05:00.450 --> 00:05:02.430
when you originally picked up the band.

00:05:02.730 --> 00:05:07.980
You can fudge and just stitch the facing
down, but doing a few short rows on the

00:05:07.980 --> 00:05:12.030
facing will give you squared corners
to completely encase the band.

00:05:12.989 --> 00:05:16.650
In the next video, we'll knit
the second side of our band.

00:05:17.010 --> 00:05:18.750
Let's think of it as a facing.

00:05:19.710 --> 00:05:25.349
We will work some short row increases
to create the corners in that facing.

